\title{envirolipids: Predict NPP from brGDGT data}
\description{
A tool to predict Net Primary Productivity (NPP) from relative abundance of individual brGDGTs using centered log-ratio (CLR) transformation and a pre-trained random forest model. Includes diagnostic tools to assess whether new samples fall within the brGDGT composition space of the training data, identifying potentially unreliable predictions. When mean annual temperature and total annual precipitation are available, the package also computes potential NPP using the Miami and Thornthwaite Memorial models, expressed by default in grams of carbon so that they are comparable with the brGDGT-based estimates.
